// bastion (ARC 5 item 26): the crafting-chain table — station kind →
// (input def, n) → (output def, n). The cook pipeline generalized to DATA
// (the thought-table pattern): the generator's raw gate, the fetch's
// required_item, and the completion's product all read THIS row, so a new
// chain is a new entry, not new Rust. v1 recipes are single-input.
//
// ITEM 29: the retired `RAW_FOOD_DEFS` const (bastion_jobs) also listed the
// four raw meats -- MEAT_{SMALL,LARGE,BIRD,TOUGH}_RAW_ITEM -- under F23's
// "a kill feed the KITCHEN rather than just the hand". No meat row was ever
// carried over to this table, so meat is NOT cookable today. Adding one is a
// deliberate behaviour change (it gives the hearth an input a failed farm
// cannot take away); it was not made when the dead const was deleted.
(
    recipes: [
        (
            station: CookStation,
            input: ("common.items.food.mushroom", 1),
            output: ("common.items.food.apple_mushroom_curry", 1),
        ),
        // Wheat is also cookable (the second FOOD_DEFS raw) — same station,
        // proving multi-recipe-per-station dispatch as data.
        (
            station: CookStation,
            input: ("common.items.bastion.wheat", 1),
            output: ("common.items.food.apple_mushroom_curry", 1),
        ),
    ],
)
